<resources>
    <!--
      AppCompat, not MaterialComponents. `WryActivity` extends `AppCompatActivity`, which needs an
      AppCompat-descended theme and nothing more. This parent was the ONLY thing pulling
      `com.google.android.material` into the APK - eight Tauri plugin modules declare the library
      from the plugin template and not one Kotlin file in any of them, or here, names a class from
      it - and it is what put `MaterialDatePicker` in the DEX, which Google Play reports as a
      deprecated `Window.setStatusBarColor` call site.

      `windowBackground` is what shows through while SvelteKit hydrates (the WebView is
      deliberately transparent - see `MainActivity.onWebViewCreate`) and what the Android 12+
      system splash paints behind the icon. It had never been set: the flash was the parent
      theme's own grey `colorBackground`, by luck rather than by choice, while `app_background`
      sat defined in two configurations and referenced by nothing. There is no `values-night`
      copy of this file: `@color/app_background` already resolves per configuration, so a second
      identical style would say nothing.
    -->
    <style name="Theme.mines_app" parent="Theme.AppCompat.DayNight.NoActionBar">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@color/app_background</item>
    </style>
</resources>
